Nevertheless, we need to construct route based on given data: The root is the molecule that was used in template searches (the target). That target is likely the product of the first reaction (template 324324). The SMILES of that product is not given directly, but we can infer from mapping: it's the same as precursor1? Actually the mapping shows product side after ">>". So we can extract product SMILES: "[CH3:1][c:2]4[cH:7][cH:6][c:5]([NH:8][S:9](=[O:10])([c:12]5[cH:17][cH:16][c:15](/[CH:18]=[CH:19]/[C:20](O)=[O:21])[cH:14][cH:13]2)=[O:11])[cH:4][cH:3]4". Convert to standard: "Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)O)cc2)cc1". So root SMILES = that.

Thus route: root mol with that SMILES, children reaction 324324, children: mol "Nc1ccccc1N" and mol "Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)O)cc2)cc1"? Wait order doesn't matter.

